 partisan lean favors Republicans by about four points. Republican Casey Askar and Democrat Pia Dandiya have raised similar sums, with Dandiya holding slightly more cash on hand. Trump has endorsed Askar, and Dandiya has begun airing general election ads.\n\nMost raters call the race Tilt or Lean Republican, though two call it a Tossup and one leans Democratic. The available polls, all conducted for Democratic sponsors, show a dead heat, with the latest giving Dandiya a two-point edge. Polymarket prices a modest Republican edge. A strong national midterm environment for Democrats offsets the district's lean, leaving this a genuine tossup with a narrow Republican edge.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.5161, "margin": 0.22}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4647, "margin": -1.0}]}